From cea20e483571039bfd13bfccd328b4c5cd334219 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:49:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 401/402] SableOS: keyboard-first focus in setup steps

On a hardware keyboard the first key press with nothing focused now lands
on the step's initial control (first text field, else Start/Next, else the
first control) instead of doing nothing; MoveHome/MoveEnd jump to the
first/last control; a held Enter/Space/Tab does not repeat an action; and
Enter in a step's last text field runs its primary action. All other keys
(arrows, Tab, Enter on a button, Back/Escape, text keys, system Home,
PageUp/PageDown, Ctrl/Meta shortcuts) keep their platform behaviour, and
any failure falls back to it, so no step can be blocked.

The decisions live in a pure SableKeyPolicy class (no android.* types),
ported from the SableOS keyboard-first setup flow reference (IR-014).
